  "final_answer": "## Why it's late\n\nWO-2026-00185 (Door Inner Panel (pressed), qty 1) is **late \u2014 3 days past due**: planned 11\u201318 Oct 2026, today 21 Oct, produced qty 0.\n\nThe only signal on it is **`not_released`** \u2014 it is still in **draft**, so it was never released to the floor. Nothing else is holding it: no material request, subcontract, stock, quality or downtime signal came back, and the platform records **no operations, no route workstations and no current job card**, so I can't tell you which machine or operation it is waiting on. Cost: expected and actual are both 0, so no cost has been recorded and no variance can be computed.\n\n## What it blocks\n\nThe platform found **45 potential consumer work orders** by BOM matching \u2014 these are \"may be affected\", not confirmed blocks, because stock or another order could cover the need. They include:\n\n- 33 door-related orders (WO-2026-00187 through WO-2026-00124) \u2014 draft/not started, many already past their planned ends.\n- WO-2026-00110, WO-2026-00095, WO-2026-00080, WO-2026-00065 (Door Module Sub-assembly), and WO-2026-00112, WO-2026-00107, WO-2026-00097, WO-2026-00092, WO-2026-00082, WO-2026-00067, WO-2026-00062, WO-2026-00052 at depth 2.\n\n**Customer impact is partly unknown.** WO-2026-00185 is make-to-order with no linked sales order, so nothing on the order itself is recorded exposure. Through the potential consumers, eight sales orders may be affected \u2014 Tata Ficosa Automotive Systems: SO-2026-00027 (\u20b920,91,356.95, due 2026-09-07), SO-2026-00192 (\u20b914,83,182.12, due 2026-07-14), SO-2026-00187 (\u20b912,08,697.60, due 2026-05-30), SO-2026-00056 (\u20b99,14,603.56, due 2026-10-06, already delivered); Kirloskar Pumps Ltd: SO-2026-00053 (\u20b93,37,155.46, due 2026-10-10, already delivered), SO-2026-00198 (\u20b92,16,054.70, due 2026-08-03), SO-2026-00164 (\u20b910,47,415.32, due 2026-06-30), SO-2026-00039 (\u20b94,49,475.88, due 2026-09-19). Treat these as **potential** exposure only.\n\n## Rescheduling\n\n**Applied:**\n- **WO-2026-00185**: 11 Oct \u2192 18 Oct becomes **21 Oct \u2192 28 Oct**.\n- **WO-2026-00186**: 22 Oct \u2192 25 Oct becomes **29 Oct \u2192 01 Nov**.\n\n**Not applied:** WO-2026-00187 was **not approved** by the platform (its planned end date needs human approval under this seat's policy), and 33 other dependants (WO-2026-00184, 00182, 00180 \u2026 00124, WO-2026-00110, WO-2026-00112, WO-2026-00107) came back **not_approved** as well. WO-2026-00187 and these dependants were still showing *writable_by_seat: true* in the proposal, so the block is at approval, not a permission gap on my side \u2014 a person needs to approve them. Six more orders \u2014 WO-2026-00095, WO-2026-00080, WO-2026-00065, WO-2026-00097, WO-2026-00092, WO-2026-00082, WO-2026-00077 \u2014 are **locked** (status \"not_started\": dates are fixed after submit and need an admin cancel), so those proposals are recommendations only. No order edited by someone else mid-run, so nothing was refused on a conflict.\n\n## Not visible to me\n\nNothing. Every entity I needed for this request was readable, and I have no reason to report a data gap other than the order having no routing/operations and no linked sales order.",
